# The routing panel on the deployed website block, prs / tim version 4.
# Captured 2026-09-10. Commit 4662a69, image main-5, run 34474243628.
# This is the first time resolveIdentity has run against a real inbound request.

# THE CLAIM UNDER TEST: the resolver's identity equals the handler's own nodeInfo.id.

$ contensis get block website main 4 --format json   (excerpt)
  "enableFullUriRouting": true, "port": 3001, "staticPaths": []
  "image": { "tag": "main-5" }
  "status": { "deployment": "deployed", "workflow": "released",
              "running": { "hq": "available", "london": "available", "manchester": "available" } }

# Two different nodes, two different identities. `/blogs` and some blog paths 404 at the
# platform, so the block is never asked about them, exactly as block-404-routing predicts.

$ curl -L -c jar -b jar -H 'x-debug: true' 'https://staging-tim-prs.cloud.contensis.com<PATH>?block-website-versionno=4'

  GET /               panel kind=id  pathname=/              id=97ad4a16-821a-4798-adcd-f17ce876538a
                      handler nodeInfo.id                    97ad4a16-821a-4798-adcd-f17ce876538a   MATCH

  GET /blogs/canvas   panel kind=id  pathname=/blogs/canvas  id=c877264a-787f-4b0d-8045-1ec8ee2d3d4e
                      handler nodeInfo.id                    c877264a-787f-4b0d-8045-1ec8ee2d3d4e   MATCH

  GET /blogs                                                 404, no debug header, not our body
  GET /blogs/the-history-of-coffee                           404, same

# pathname is the FRIENDLY URL here. Under `contensis dev requests` the same request
# arrives as `/`. That contrast is the entire argument for routing on the header, and it
# is why a path-dispatching app passes locally and fails deployed.

# --- FINDINGS THE PANEL SURFACED, all contradicting current .knowledge claims ---

# 1. x-alias IS forwarded to the block. Value observed: prs
#    .knowledge/contensis-request-handler-contract.md:60 and EXPLORATION.md list it as
#    denied. The handler source's DisallowedRequestHeaderMappings does not contain it.
#    The conclusion "take alias from config" still stands on other grounds, but the
#    stated reason is wrong.

# 2. x-forwarded-proto and traceparent ARE forwarded despite being on the denylist.
#    x-forwarded-proto: https
#    traceparent: 00-e657779597c68f4664c5812be7d4c098-832d4085c2d1701e-00
#    traceparent was already known to leak (the .NET HttpClient adds its own).
#    x-forwarded-proto is new.

# 3. The x-requires-* hints arrive INBOUND as "true" without the client sending them.
#    Present: x-requires-alias, -project-api-id, -node-id, -entry-id, -block-id
#    Absent:  x-requires-entry-language, -version-no
#    The contract says these are a client opt-in that carries no inbound value. The
#    handler sets five of them itself.

# 4. The block runtime environment, previously unrecorded. Both casings are set:
#    alias=prs  ALIAS=prs  projectId=tim  PROJECT=tim  PROJECT_API_ID=tim
#    NODE_ENV=production
#    plus BLOCK_BRANCH_ID, BLOCK_VERSION_ID, BLOCK_VERSION_COMMIT_ID,
#    BLOCK_VERSION_IMAGE_URL, DATA_CENTER, CONTENSIS_CLIENT_ID, HOSTNAME and the
#    Kubernetes service vars. A block CAN read its own alias and project from env.

# 5. Other headers arriving, names only (the panel withholds their values):
#    content-length, cookie, delivery-project, surrogate-key, use-modern-cache-logic,
#    x-block-request, x-entry-versionstatus, x-forwarded-for, x-geoip-country-code,
#    x-node-versionstatus, x-orig-host
#    delivery-project, x-entry-versionstatus and x-node-versionstatus look
#    routing-relevant and are not in any documented list. Values not yet captured.

# 6. Confirmed as predicted: window.ContensisEntryId is emitted empty on a post-cutoff
#    block, so the entry id must come from x-entry-id.
#    ContensisProjectApiId=tim ContensisAlias=prs ContensisSso=false
#    ContensisEntryVersionStatus=published ContensisEntryId=empty ("")
#    ContensisEntryLanguage=en-GB ContensisVersionNumber=17.2.1.53
#    The globals being filled also proves the client module loaded, i.e. the per-version
#    asset prefix rewrite worked for this build.

